<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_criticalstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Recklessness</span></a> with the 4-piece can lead to some interesting choices in raids. Often, it's gonna be better to use it on cooldown so it lines up with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=114207/skull-banner">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/warrior_skullbanner.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skull Banner</span></a>, but in some instances, you might want to delay your use of Recklessness to line up with boss damage amplification windows.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Fury Warrior Trinkets in Phase 1</span></h2>DPS trinkets tend to be very straightforward. When it comes to the best DPS trinkets in phase 1, there are clear winners and losers. There are, unfortunately, no competitive on-use trinkets in Phase 1, so you will be aiming to run two proc trinkets.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Warriors should typically use one on-use and one passive trinket, or two passive trinkets, but rarely ever two on-use.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86042/jade-charioteer-figurine">
<img alt="Jade Charioteer Figurine" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_mount_ridinghorse.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jade Charioteer Figurine</span></a> is the only notable on-use trinket in Phase 1, but it is unfortunately very weak. While it provides a solid baseline amount of Strength, the on-use effect grants Haste, the weakest secondary stat for Fury Warriors. Haste notoriously scales poorly for Warriors, especially in AoE situations, where on-use trinkets are typically preferred due to the ability to time burst damage.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87072/lei-shens-final-orders">
<img alt="Lei Shen's Final Orders" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lei Shen's Final Orders</span></a> is Fury Warriors best trinket option in Phase 1. It offers a very strong 15-second Strength proc and a strong amount of Haste baseline, which can be reforged into Critical Strike. The trinket has a 15% chance to proc from attacks and has a 55-second internal cooldown.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87172/darkmist-vortex">
<img alt="Darkmist Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_cyclone_nodebris.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmist Vortex</span></a> is the second-best trinket option in Phase 1. It offers a large amount of Haste for 20 seconds when procced, and has a strong baseline amount of Strength. It has a 15% chance to proc each time one of your attacks hits, and has an internal cooldown of 115 seconds.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> is the third-best trinket option for Fury Warriors in Phase 1. It offers a strong 15-second Strength proc and a strong baseline Strength value. Relic of Xuen has a 20% proc chance from melee attacks and a 55-second internal cooldown. Keep in mind that this bind-on-equip trinket is likely to be very expensive early in Mists of Pandaria due to high demand and the fact that it can only be crafted through the Inscription profession.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81138/carbonic-carbuncle">
<img alt="Carbonic Carbuncle" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Carbonic Carbuncle</span></a> is Fury Warriors fourth-best option in Phase 1. Although it only sits at a 463 item level, it's still incredibly powerful for Fury Warriors due to its 30-second-long Critical Strike proc. The trinket has a 15% chance to proc from attacks and has a 115-second internal cooldown.</div></li></ul>
